From a4e82fbc61afb4042cc9c3d33247ba2eb5c8792f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: 77ph <tk@itarragon.net>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 16:45:53 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 6/7] feat(operator): direct calls of a Kernel agent account
 through agent-signer

ADAPTATION item 8: the agent's direct (non-Safe) calls -- ERC-8004
setMetadata from IdentityPublisher and the SolverNet metadata publisher --
go through the hardware-signed Kernel account when config.signer is set.

- tx-retry: markUserOperationWallet / isUserOperationWallet. A marked wallet
  is sent once under the account's broadcast lock (the venue's lock when one
  is installed, shared with the Kernel's Safe transactions), with no EOA
  nonce ledger, fee bumps, stuck-nonce eviction or resends: the signer owns
  nonce, fees and inclusion, and only it can tell whether an unknown outcome
  landed. Unmarked wallets keep the EOA path unchanged.
- signer: createAgentSignerWalletClient -- the Kernel's json-rpc account over
  the agent-signer transport, marked.
- main.ts: with config.signer, IdentityPublisher and the SolverNet publisher
  use it. The Kernel must own the agent NFT (a one-time transfer).
- tests: the tx-retry path (single send without nonce/fee fields, no resend,
  serialization, no RPC use) and the wallet; the Kernel-owner hermetic loop
  now moves the agent NFT to the Kernel and publishes ERC-8004 metadata
  through the daemon's publisher via agent-signer, read back from the
  registry.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
